  "Id": 2016,
  "Title": "Happy Healthcare Simulation Week 2019",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "CIME joined the global simulation community to celebrate Healthcare Simulation Week 2019. The aim was to generate awareness of the importance of simulation in improving the safety, effectiveness, and efficiency of healthcare delivery.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "CIME joined the global simulation community to celebrate Healthcare Simulation Week 2019, from 16-20 September. The aim was to generate awareness of the importance of simulation in improving the safety, effectiveness, and efficiency of healthcare delivery. CIME organised the following activities:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. Room of Errors"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. Hands-only CPR"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The room of errors was to help participants to be more observant of hazards in the home and to develop their situational awareness. Participants were given 30 seconds to enter the simulated room, Virtual Reality or Actual; make a mental note of their assessment then withdraw and list the hazards they witnessed. A BIG congratulations to Amyn Deedar Ali, Nurse Instructor, Nephrology Urology, Rozina Rashid, Nurse, Home Health Programme, and Shafi Ullah, Nursing Student BScN Year II for wining this competition."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The CPR simulation activity was held at the Sports Centre to generate awareness among the general public about how they can save lives through hands-only CPR. Volunteers were taught about the emergency measures to be taken and how to perform a hands-only CPR. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mr qaSIM had fun with students throughout the week. After spending his precious time with students at CIME, he finally had a chance to tour our campus. He went out of CIME to celebrate healthcare simulation week, students got a chance to take selfies with him and he did enjoy Karachi's lovely weather!!! He toured AKU in the campus shuttle. Let's watch his tour video. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
